Case 01 — Consistent Supporting Evidence- Reject

case_id: GEA-001

gene: SYN1

synthetic_variant: SYN1:c.250A>G

context:
Educational case designed to test whether multiple independent evidence items consistently support the same direction of interpretation.

evidence_items:

Population dataset: variant is reported at very low frequency in the synthetic reference population.
Functional study: synthetic cell-based assay reports substantially reduced protein activity compared with the reference sequence.
Computational analysis: three synthetic prediction tools indicate a potentially disruptive effect.
Experimental study: an independent synthetic assay reports a similar reduction in protein function.

source_label:
SYNTHETIC_POPULATION_01, SYNTHETIC_FUNCTIONAL_01, SYNTHETIC_COMPUTATIONAL_01, SYNTHETIC_FUNCTIONAL_02

missing_fields:

Exact experimental conditions for one functional assay
Independent replication details

conflicts:
None identified.
Case 02 — Consistent Non-Supporting Evidence- Modify

case_id: GEA-002

gene: SYN2

synthetic_variant: SYN2:c.812G>T

context:
Educational case testing whether the system can recognize that available evidence does not support a proposed functional effect.

evidence_items:

Population dataset: variant occurs relatively frequently in the synthetic reference population.
Functional assay: synthetic protein-expression experiment reports no meaningful difference from reference.
Independent functional assay: synthetic activity assay reports activity within the predefined reference range.
Computational predictions: results are mixed but do not provide consistent evidence of functional disruption.

source_label:
SYNTHETIC_POPULATION_02, SYNTHETIC_FUNCTIONAL_03, SYNTHETIC_FUNCTIONAL_04, SYNTHETIC_COMPUTATIONAL_02

missing_fields:

Additional independent functional experiments
Detailed population stratification

conflicts:
No major conflict. Computational predictions differ from one another but are not directly contradictory experimental findings.
Case 03 — Critical Missing Evidence- Accept

case_id: GEA-003

gene: SYN3

synthetic_variant: SYN3:c.1045C>T

context:
Educational case testing whether the system recognizes that an evidence packet is incomplete rather than filling the gap with an assumption.

